### Check for existing issues - [x] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ### What happened? `reasoning_effort` values `minimal`, `none`, and `disable` all fail with HTTP 400 on `vertex_ai/gemini-3.7-flash`: ``` "message": "Thinking level is unsupported: THINKING_LEVEL_MINIMAL", "status": "INVALID_ARGUMENT" ``` All three map to `thinkingLevel: "minimal"`, which Vertex rejects for `gemini-3.7-flash`. `low`, `medium`, and `high` work fine, and `minimal` works fine on `gemini-3.6-flash` and `gemini-3.5-flash` — so this is specific to 3.7, not the family. The eligibility test for the minimal thinking level is a substring match: ```python # litellm/llms/vertex_ai/gemini/vertex_and_google_ai_studio_gemini.py:861 is_gemini3flash: Final = model and ("flash" in model.lower() and "gemini-3" in model.lower()) ``` `gemini-3.7-flash` satisfies it, so `minimal` is sent. The comment above it says the test covers "any future 3.x-flash variants" — that assumption does not hold for 3.7. **Expected:** all documented `reasoning_effort` values return 200 for `gemini-3.7-flash`, resolving to a thinking level Vertex accepts (`low` is the floor for this model). Three of six values being a hard 400 makes `reasoning_effort` unusable for any caller that can't special-case this one model. Affects `1.97.0` and current `main`. Same substring test in `v1.98.0-rc.1`, `v1.96.2`, `v1.95.1`, `v1.93.2`, `v1.91.5`, and `v1.89.1` — no version excludes 3.7. Note `/v1/messages` with `thinking.budget_tokens` is **not** affected: that path only sets a thinking level when `enable_gemini_default_thinking_level_low` is opted into, and it defaults to `False`. ### User Flow Before a (hypothetical) fix: a user picking the lowest reasoning setting on gemini-3.7-flash gets a hard error instead of an answer. 1. They send POST http://localhost:4001/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "gemini-3.7-flash"` and `"reasoning_effort": "minimal"` 2. They get back HTTP 400 with `"Thinking level is unsupported: THINKING_LEVEL_MINIMAL"` and no assistant message 3. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "none"` — HTTP 400, identical message 4. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "disable"` — HTTP 400, identical message 5. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "low"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message 6. They send the same POST with `"model": "gemini-3.6-flash"` and `"reasoning_effort": "minimal"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message, so the setting they wanted works on the neighbouring model and only gemini-3.7-flash refuses it After a (hypothetical) fix: the same user makes the same six requests and every one returns an answer. 1. They send POST http://localhost:4001/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "gemini-3.7-flash"` and `"reasoning_effort": "minimal"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message 2. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "none"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message 3. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "disable"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message 4. They retry the same POST with `"reasoning_effort": "low"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message 5. They send the same POST with `"model": "gemini-3.6-flash"` and `"reasoning_effort": "minimal"` — HTTP 200 with an assistant message ### Proof the bug occurs **Config / setup the proxy ran with:** `config.yaml` — no `litellm_settings`, no callbacks, nothing custom: ```yaml model_list: # The affected model - model_name: gemini-3.7-flash litellm_params: model: vertex_ai/gemini-3.7-flash vertex_location: global vertex_project: os.environ/VERTEXAI_PROJECT vertex_credentials: os.environ/VERTEXAI_CREDENTIALS # Controls: same family, accept the minimal thinking level - model_name: gemini-3.6-flash litellm_params: model: vertex_ai/gemini-3.6-flash vertex_location: global vertex_project: os.environ/VERTEXAI_PROJECT vertex_credentials: os.environ/VERTEXAI_CREDENTIALS - model_name: gemini-3.5-flash litellm_params: model: vertex_ai/g