## Check for existing issues - [x] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ## What happened? A model group whose name contains a slash, which is the normal shape for OpenRouter style and other provider prefixed names, is listed by `GET /v1/models` under that exact id but cannot be retrieved at `GET /v1/models/{model_id}`. The gateway answers `404 {"detail":"Not Found"}`, which is the same body it returns for a URL it does not serve, so a client cannot tell the model apart from a missing endpoint. Percent encoding the slash does not help, the encoded form comes back 404 as well. I expected retrieve to accept any id that the listing hands out, the way the OpenAI API does. The same request works for model names without a slash, so the failure follows the name and not the configuration. #32770 reports the same shape of failure on `GET`/`DELETE /fallback/{model}` and the fix proposed there does not reach this route. ## User Flow Before a (hypothetical) fix: a developer pointing an OpenAI compatible client at the gateway cannot confirm that a slash named model exists, so their client treats it as unavailable 1. They send GET http://litellm-domain/v1/models with their key and get one entry back, `"id": "mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct"` 2. Their client retrieves that exact id, GET http://litellm-domain/v1/models/mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct 3. The gateway answers `404` with `{"detail":"Not Found"}`, the same body it gives for a URL it does not serve 4. They retry with the slash percent encoded, GET http://litellm-domain/v1/models/mistralai%2Fmistral-7b-instruct, and get the same `404` 5. They try the unversioned form, GET http://litellm-domain/models/mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct, and get the same `404` 6. Their client marks the model unavailable and never sends it a request, although POST http://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct"` routes to the provider normally After a (hypothetical) 